"prose": [
{
"from": 220,
"to": 230,
"text": "The gates: - escher-driver's unit tests; - `stand_layout` and the blitz-tests companions the diff moves: `stand_actions`, `stand_cross_os_readings`,   `stand_act_spans`, `stand_mcp_tools`, `stand_replay`; - seven_guis' four process checks; - the capability-statement pin; - the pre-push gate (`fast`); - the `doc` leg. The chunk edits public doc comments (`Placer`, `Session::layout`, `Command`, `Outcome`, `FieldKind`,   the crate doc), and `fast` runs no rustdoc (test-plan · decision/doc-leg-gates-public-doc-edits; the operator's   directive, inputs#I2); - `stand-repeat`."
},
{
"from": 232,
"to": 235,
"text": "No boot-path touchpoint changes a binary's start. `host_log`, `mcp_log`, `mcp_server` and `cli_commands` drive both binaries' roles and stand in for the smoke. There is no live leg: the cold-agent pipe is not run, nor changed (F1, inputs#I3). The coverage leg is not run locally. CI's coverage job reads escher-driver's 97 % floor on the pushed tree, and the CI read below asserts green over it."
},
{
"from": 237,
"to": 245,
"text": "Each new check is controlled red-before-green (tests S3). After the steps are green, /implement makes three one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries: - **The unexplained word reverted.** In `layout.rs`, `unexplained()` answers `Placer::Engine(PlacedBy::Block)` again.   Fired on the escher-driver unit entry, case `an_unexplained_element_reads_its_bounds_and_layout_causes`. - **The verb reaching a step.** The `Command::Layout` arm in `execute.rs` calls the harness's `pump()` before the   read. Fired on the `stand_layout` entry, case: step 8's no-change test, which must read the delivered ticks   applied. - **Exploration's filter by kind removed.** In `explore.rs`, `explorable` checks the image kind alone again. Fired   on the escher-driver unit entry, case: step 6's explored-set test."
},
{
"from": 247,
"to": 247,
"text": "Each control names the edit's text and the case by its test name (gate-contract.md §Control)."
},
{
"from": 249,
"to": 251,
"text": "An acceptance reads CI. The windows and macOS legs of `matrix_test` hold the re-read digests, and CI's coverage job holds the floor. So the operator's hygiene, push and CI entries stand. The diff is OS-sensitive only through those digests: no `cfg` site is added or changed. The `ci.py` entry's note names them."
}
],
